ential HLA-A2 binding peptides based on independent binding of individual peptide side chains. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>152</volume>:<fpage>163</fpage>&#x02013;175.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8254189</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rammensee, H., J. Bachmann, N.P. Emmerich, O.A. Bachor, and S. Stevanovic. <year>1999</year>. SYFPEITHI: database for MHC ligands and peptide motifs. <source>Immunogenetics.</source> <volume>50</volume>:<fpage>213</fpage>&#x02013;219.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10602881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bednarek, M.A., S.Y. Sauma, M.C. Gammon, G. Porter, S. Tamhanker, A.R. Williamson, and H.J. Zweerink. <year>1991</year>. The minimum peptide epitope from the influenza matrixprotein. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>147</volume>:<fpage>4047</fpage>&#x02013;4053.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1721637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Altman, J.D., P.A. Moss, P.J. Goulder, D.H. Barouch, M.G. McHeyzer-Williams, J.I. Bell, A.J. McMichael, and M.M. Davis. <year>1996</year>. Phenotypic analysis of antigen-specific T lymphocytes. <source>Science.</source> <volume>274</volume>:<fpage>94</fpage>&#x02013;96.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8810254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal">Propato, A., E. Schiaffella, E. Vicenzi, V. Francavilla, L. Baloni, M. Paroli, L. Finocchi, N. Tanigaki, S. Ghezzi, R. Ferrara, et al. <year>2001</year>. Spreading of HIV-specific CD8<sup>+</sup> T-cell repertoire in long-term nonprogressors and its role in the control of viral load and disease activity. <source>Hum. Immunol.</source> <volume>62</volume>:<fpage>561</fpage>&#x02013;576.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11390031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kang, X., Y. Kawankami, M. el